<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:docs="using:Fili.Theme.MudAvalonia.Gallery.Docs"
             x:Class="Fili.Theme.MudAvalonia.Gallery.Docs.Pages.ReducedMotionPage">
  <StackPanel Classes="doc">
    <docs:DocHeader Title="Reduced motion"
                    Summary="One key stops what the theme moves or fades on its own, for people whose system or settings ask for less motion, all but the one sign that work is going on. MudBlazor has no such switch." />

    <TextBlock Classes="body1 p">
      <Run Text="Set " /><Run Classes="code" Text="FiliReducedMotion" /><Run Text=" to True in the application's resources, from your app's own setting. It can change at any time, and reaches every window and popup." />
    </TextBlock>
    <docs:CodeBlock Code="&lt;Application.Resources&gt;&#10;  &lt;x:Boolean x:Key=&quot;FiliReducedMotion&quot;&gt;True&lt;/x:Boolean&gt;&#10;&lt;/Application.Resources&gt;"
                    Margin="0,0,0,16" />

    <TextBlock Classes="h5 section" Text="What stops" />
    <TextBlock Classes="body1 p" Text="The ripple on a press. The fade of a popup, a menu and a tooltip. A skeleton's pulse and wave. A snackbar's slide in and out. An expansion panel's grow and an overlay's fade, which show at once. A tab indicator's slide, which jumps to the new tab. A striped progress bar's sliding bands, which stand still." />
    <TextBlock Classes="body1 p" Text="And every transition the theme declares, each of which now happens at once: a drawer opening and shutting, a switch's thumb crossing its track, a field's label floating up and its focus underline drawing, an expander's or a tree row's chevron turning, the margin an expansion panel opens round itself, a determinate circular progress reaching a new value, a data grid's sort arrow turning, a slider's value label showing, and the fade of a hover or a selection's colour." />

    <TextBlock Classes="h5 section" Text="What keeps moving" />
    <TextBlock Classes="body1 p" Text="An indeterminate progress indicator, linear or circular: its movement is the only sign that work is going on. Transitions an app declares on its own controls are the app's, and the key leaves them alone." />

    <TextBlock Classes="h5 section" Text="The system's setting" />
    <TextBlock Classes="body1 p" Text="The theme does not follow the operating system's reduce-motion setting on its own, and Avalonia 12.1 does not report it: its platform settings carry the system's colours and contrast preference, not motion. An app that wants to follow the system reads the setting itself, through the platform's own API, and sets the key; an app setting of its own is the portable way." />

    <TextBlock Classes="h5 section" Text="Where it is read" />
    <TextBlock Classes="body1 p" Text="Each window reads the key once, from its own resources or the application's, and passes it to everything inside it and to the popups it opens. A key in a panel's resources inside a window does nothing: set it on the application, or on a window of its own." />
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
